# Line endings are part of the evidence here.
#
# The protocol lock records a SHA-256 for each tracked JSON Schema, and the
# published tables and figures are compared byte for byte against regenerated
# copies. A checkout that rewrites line endings changes those bytes, so on a
# Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` all five schema digests
# disagree with the lock and `make lock-check` stops the run — on a repository
# that is in fact intact.
#
# Normalise to LF in the working tree on every platform, which is what the
# recorded digests were taken over.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Everything a digest or a byte comparison is taken over: never transformed,
# on checkout or on commit, whatever the platform or the local Git config.
results/** -text
